---Cluster kube-proxy customization: iptables and ipvs configurations can both be set at the same time, kube-proxy will use the one according to the cluster's kubeProxyMode value
---@class ovh.cloud.CloudProjectKubeCustomizationKubeProxy
---@field iptables? ovh.cloud.CloudProjectKubeCustomizationKubeProxyIptables|distilled.Null Kubernetes cluster kube-proxy customization of iptables specific config (durations format is RFC3339 duration, e.g. 'PT60S')
---@field ipvs? ovh.cloud.CloudProjectKubeCustomizationKubeProxyIpvs|distilled.Null Kubernetes cluster kube-proxy customization of ipvs specific config (durations format is RFC3339 duration, e.g. 'PT60S')

---Configuration used when kube-proxy is configured with iptables mode (durations format is RFC3339 duration, e.g. 'PT60S')
---@class ovh.cloud.CloudProjectKubeCustomizationKubeProxyIptables
---@field minSyncPeriod? string|distilled.Null minSyncPeriod is the minimum period that iptables rules are refreshed, in RFC3339 duration format (e.g. 'PT60S')
---@field syncPeriod? string|distilled.Null syncPeriod is the period that iptables rules are refreshed, in RFC3339 duration format (e.g. 'PT60S'). Must be greater than 0

---Configuration used when kube-proxy is configured with ipvs mode (durations format is RFC3339 duration, e.g. 'PT60S')
---@class ovh.cloud.CloudProjectKubeCustomizationKubeProxyIpvs
---@field minSyncPeriod? string|distilled.Null minSyncPeriod is the minimum period that ipvs rules are refreshed in RFC3339 duration format (e.g. 'PT60S')
---@field scheduler? ovh.cloud.CloudKubeKubeProxyIpvsSchedulerEnum|string|distilled.Null ipvs scheduler
---@field syncPeriod? string|distilled.Null syncPeriod is the period that ipvs rules are refreshed in RFC3339 duration format (e.g. 'PT60S'). Must be greater than 0
---@field tcpFinTimeout? string|distilled.Null tcpFinTimeout is the timeout value used for IPVS TCP sessions after receiving a FIN in RFC3339 duration format (e.g. 'PT60S'). The default value is 'PT0S', which preserves the current timeout value on the system
---@field tcpTimeout? string|distilled.Null tcpTimeout is the timeout value used for idle IPVS TCP sessions in RFC3339 duration format (e.g. 'PT60S'). The default value is 'PT0S', which preserves the current timeout value on the system. Cannot be set between 'PT0S' and 'PT5S', in order to prevent in-cluster networking issues.
---@field udpTimeout? string|distilled.Null udpTimeout is the timeout value used for IPVS UDP packets in RFC3339 duration format (e.g. 'PT60S'). The default value is 'PT0S', which preserves the current timeout value on the system

